        "comments": "The assembly cjAnaOrca4.2 is based on 37x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The HiC data used for curation is from a different individual to the pacbio. There are two examples where the HiC suggests a change to the assembly is required but the pacbio reads suggests no change (no gaps over these locations, fully assembled through). For these locations (chromosome 1\n89,509 Kbp and chromosome 2\n55,711-56,152 Kbp), we decided to follow the original pacbio assembly rather than make the change based on the HiC signal.",
